WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.568 --> 00:00:01.808
The next morning in school I told Mrs.

2
00:00:01.828 --> 00:00:03.529
Romano about my new invention.

3
00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:05.669
Then I showed her Molly's pink flower.

4
00:00:05.729 --> 00:00:07.210
"Why, Iggy," she said.

5
00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.270
"What a marvelous idea!"

6
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:14.192
"Can I put the flower on your glasses?"

7
00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:14.592
I asked.

8
00:00:31.752 --> 00:00:36.376
Mrs. Romano nodded so I wrapped the wire stem around the frames of her glasses.

9
00:00:38.658 --> 00:00:43.482
When she put the glasses on, everyone started laughing.

10
00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:47.806
"Mrs. Romano, you look funny with a flower sticking up from your glasses!"

11
00:00:48.246 --> 00:00:48.867
cried Evan.

12
00:00:48.887 --> 00:00:52.970
"Well, at least I won't lose them," said Mrs.

13
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.311
Romano, smiling.

14
00:00:55.652 --> 00:00:56.233
But when Mrs.

15
00:00:56.293 --> 00:00:59.636
Romano went to feed the goldfish, the flower fell off her glasses.

16
00:01:00.604 --> 00:01:02.605
It tumbled right into the fish tank!

17
00:01:05.485 --> 00:01:07.166
Lauren scooped it out.

18
00:01:07.186 --> 00:01:11.347
"Iggy!" cried Molly.

19
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:14.528
"You promised to take care of my flower.

20
00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.048
You didn't tell me it was going to get wet!"

21
00:01:17.068 --> 00:01:20.769
"I'm sorry," I said.

22
00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.770
"I didn't think it would fall into the fish tank."

23
00:01:25.591 --> 00:01:30.112
We put the flower on a sunny windowsill during art class so it would dry.

24
00:01:31.552 --> 00:01:33.633
When we came back from art, Mrs.

25
00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:37.655
Romano suggested that someone else try the Fabulous Glasses-Finder.

26
00:01:37.676 --> 00:01:40.017
"Let me try it!"

27
00:01:40.397 --> 00:01:41.197
said Kristin.

28
00:01:42.918 --> 00:01:45.640
That's when things really started to go wrong.

29
00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.823
First the flower fell over Kristin's eyes and she couldn't see.

30
00:01:51.643 --> 00:01:54.145
She bumped into a desk and nearly fell over.

31
00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:58.067
Then the wire stem kept sticking her in the head.

32
00:01:58.087 --> 00:02:01.857
"Ouch," said Kristin, rubbing her head.

33
00:02:01.877 --> 00:02:03.858
"This thing hurts."

34
00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:08.441
Soon Kristin got tired of wearing the flower on her glasses.

35
00:02:09.581 --> 00:02:11.382
Lauren said she would wear it next.

36
00:02:14.044 --> 00:02:16.946
I attached the flower to Lauren's glasses at recess.

37
00:02:20.147 --> 00:02:23.609
She was in line for the slide when she leaned over to tie her shoe.

38
00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:28.032
That's when the flower stem got caught on Ruby's sweater.

39
00:02:29.428 --> 00:02:32.270
"Help! We're stuck together!"

40
00:02:32.431 --> 00:02:34.452
cried Ruby, trying to step away.

41
00:02:34.472 --> 00:02:37.134
"Stand still!"

42
00:02:37.575 --> 00:02:38.436
cried Lauren.

43
00:02:38.456 --> 00:02:41.338
"You're pulling my glasses off."

44
00:02:42.759 --> 00:02:44.480
"And you're ripping my sweater!"

45
00:02:45.041 --> 00:02:45.762
said Ruby.

46
00:02:46.802 --> 00:02:49.144
I finally got Ruby and Lauren unstuck.

47
00:02:50.325 --> 00:02:53.928
After that, Lauren didn't want to wear the flower on her glasses anymore.

48
00:02:53.948 --> 00:02:58.232
"That flower is nothing but trouble," she said.

49
00:02:59.348 --> 00:03:01.830
I hated to admit it, but Lauren was right.

50
00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:06.112
The Fabulous Glasses-Finder was not my greatest invention.

51
00:03:07.073 --> 00:03:08.774
In fact, it was one of my worst!

52
00:03:10.635 --> 00:03:13.837
The next day in school, we wrote down our invention ideas for Mr.

53
00:03:13.877 --> 00:03:19.901
Bright. He was going to announce the winner at the school assembly.

54
00:03:20.941 --> 00:03:25.044
Mrs. Romano said we could write down two invention ideas if we wanted to.

55
00:03:26.112 --> 00:03:29.154
But I didn't even have one invention I was excited about.

56
00:03:29.174 --> 00:03:32.015
I raised my hand.

57
00:03:32.035 --> 00:03:34.116
"Yes, Iggy?"

58
00:03:34.597 --> 00:03:35.117
said Mrs.

59
00:03:35.197 --> 00:03:40.600
Romano. "I don't have a good invention to write about," I said.

60
00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.622
"What about your Fabulous Glasses-Finder?"

61
00:03:45.082 --> 00:03:45.642
said Mrs.

62
00:03:45.723 --> 00:03:49.885
Romano. "It's a very original invention, Iggy."

63
00:03:49.905 --> 00:03:53.367
"Except that no one liked it," I mumbled.

64
00:03:53.387 --> 00:03:55.668
"It doesn't work that great."

65
00:03:56.588 --> 00:03:59.009
By now I was feeling a little sorry for myself.

66
00:03:59.029 --> 00:04:02.771
"I liked it," said Mrs.

67
00:04:02.871 --> 00:04:06.472
Romano. "Even though it did fall into the fish tank."

68
00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:08.433
I knew Mrs.

69
00:04:08.493 --> 00:04:10.974
Romano was only trying to make me feel better.

70
00:04:12.695 --> 00:04:15.676
But I wrote about the Fabulous Glasses-Finder anyway.

71
00:04:16.697 --> 00:04:19.358
Ruby wrote about a rubber glove filled with sand.

72
00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:23.960
You could bend the fingers to hold rings or notes.

73
00:04:25.744 --> 00:04:28.466
Evan had an idea for an automatic fish-feeder.

74
00:04:28.486 --> 00:04:34.069
"You can feed your fish, even if you're away on vacation," he explained.

75
00:04:34.089 --> 00:04:38.191
"That's a really neat idea," said Colby.

76
00:04:39.291 --> 00:04:40.592
"Very inventive!"

77
00:04:40.992 --> 00:04:41.673
agreed Mrs.

78
00:04:41.753 --> 00:04:49.738
Romano. Molly wrote about a way to cut socks and use them as hand-warmers.

79
00:04:49.758 --> 00:04:55.134
And I, Iggy, wrote about a stupid glasses-finder that no one wanted to use!
